Integrated study of functional films and interfaces (@mat-integrated-functional: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @materials-engineering, #source "../sources/Atomic-Layer-Deposition-Chemistry-and-Evidence.lingua#r_43RJYA2HWF0DWTRB766G062RHV", #materials-engineering "Defend-the-integrated-materials-investigations.lingua#r_4SGGJ7V1GYFGDYZNKVPAB5DAXM") { r_5MTVZKQD6SKNNR4J2W80C0274Y
**Read:** [Atomic layer deposition — surface chemistry and evidence](../sources/Atomic-Layer-Deposition-Chemistry-and-Evidence.lingua#r_43RJYA2HWF0DWTRB766G062RHV), full review and the accessible primary deposition investigation it identifies; earlier electronic/ionic transport, contacts, dielectric/optical response, surface preparation and degradation. Use the relevant whole solid-state and processing books.

Follow a deposited functional film from precursor delivery and surface reactions through thickness, composition, defects and interfaces to a measured response. Distinguish an ideal cycle's saturation argument from an experimentally demonstrated process window. Surface area, transport, nucleation delay, contamination and substrate conditions can alter the result.

Choose one functional quantity with sufficiently complete public evidence. Reconstruct its measurement and separate bulk-film effects from contacts, geometry and interfacial layers. Derive a simple independent limiting model, then test where it fails. Do not infer an unmeasured electrical property from an image merely because the film looks uniform.

**Deliver:** A reproducible account connecting at least one process observation to state and function, with competing explanations and a discriminating measurement. Predict a changed thickness, substrate or service condition with explicit limits. Compare precursor use, equipment, energy, yield and recoverability using available evidence. If the selected sources do not support a complete device comparison, identify the exact additional measurement needed and defend the narrower conclusion.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
**Continue in materials engineering:** [Defend the integrated materials investigations](Defend-the-integrated-materials-investigations.lingua#r_4SGGJ7V1GYFGDYZNKVPAB5DAXM).

